{
  "an3.53:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.53 ",
  "an3.53:0.2": "6. Brahmins ",
  "an3.53:0.3": "A Certain Brahmin ",
  "an3.53:1.1": "Then a brahmin went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. Seated to one side he said to the Buddha: ",
  "an3.53:1.2": "“Worthy Gotama, they speak of ‘a teaching apparent in the present life’. ",
  "an3.53:1.3": "In what way is the teaching apparent in the present life, immediately effective, inviting inspection, relevant, so that sensible people can know it for themselves?” ",
  "an3.53:2.1": "“A greedy person, overcome and overwhelmed by greed, intends to hurt themselves, hurt others, and hurt both. They experience mental pain and sadness. ",
  "an3.53:2.2": "When greed has been given up, they don’t intend to hurt themselves, hurt others, and hurt both. They don’t experience mental pain and sadness. ",
  "an3.53:2.3": "",
  "an3.53:2.4": "",
  "an3.53:2.5": "",
  "an3.53:2.6": "",
  "an3.53:2.7": "This is how the teaching is apparent in the present life, immediately effective, inviting inspection, relevant, so that sensible people can know it for themselves. ",
  "an3.53:3.1": "A hateful person, overcome by hate, intends to hurt themselves, hurt others, and hurt both. They experience mental pain and sadness. ",
  "an3.53:3.2": "When hate has been given up, they don’t intend to hurt themselves, hurt others, and hurt both. They don’t experience mental pain and sadness. ",
  "an3.53:3.3": "This, too, is how the teaching is apparent in the present li